What is the output of the following Java program featuring an unannotated interface?
```java
interface StringFilter {
    boolean test(String s);
}
public class FilterApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        StringFilter filter = s -> s.length() > 3;
        System.out.println(filter.test("Java") + " " + filter.test("C"));
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program?
```java
@FunctionalInterface
interface MathOperation {
    int apply(int a, int b);
    default int applyTwice(int a, int b) {
        return apply(apply(a, b), b);
    }
    static int identity() { return 0; }
}
public class MathApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        MathOperation add = (x, y) -> x + y;
        System.out.println(add.applyTwice(5, 10));
    }
}
```

